Subject: [PATCH 1/2] zle: a private reader mailbox, reader events and a pre-EOF decision

Adds a mailbox the line editor reads at every key-sequence boundary and while it waits for a key,
so a request can reach the reader thread without a keystroke and without the reader blocking on
anything but its own input. The reader answers it in place: it publishes what its own queues hold,
installs and accepts a line immediately, and ends a pending key wait without losing the edit
buffer. It also reports when the reader starts and stops, and takes an end-of-file decision
immediately before ZLE's empty-EOF branch, so the character is judged before either EOF branch
runs and the user's IGNORE_EOF setting is left exactly as it was.

This patch is a derivative work of Zsh and carries the Zsh licence; see shells/zsh/LICENSE.

